{{Quote|The sensors are placed. I'm going back.|[[Han Solo]], to [[Luke Skywalker]]|<ref name="ESB">{{Film|V}}</ref>}}
A '''sensor''' was one of a wide range of complex devices that helped gather information about a given subject. Sensors could range from simple handheld devices to more complex technology like [[tachyon]] detectors found on [[starship]]s.<ref name="YT1300">''[[YT-1300 Millennium Falcon Owners' Workshop Manual]]''</ref><ref name="Rebel Starfighters Owners' Workshop Manual">''[[Rebel Starfighters Owners' Workshop Manual]]''</ref>

==Description==
Sensors could operate by a variety of different methods, such as detecting [[electromagnetic radiation]], [[Gravity|gravitational]] disturbances, nuclear forces, or [[subspace]]. Sensors may detect objects by motion or vibration, through changes in [[Temperature|heat]] or pressure, or by sniffing out trace chemicals. Despite their advanced nature, sensors could be fooled by natural phenomenon including [[Star|solar]] [[radiation]], [[hydrogen]] clouds, and [[asteroid field]]s. They could also be defeated by [[electronic countermeasures]] such as [[sensor jammer]]s and [[cloaking device]]s.<ref name="YT1300" /><ref name="Cross">''[[Star Wars: The Force Awakens: Incredible Cross-Sections]]''</ref> Ships such as the [[VCX-100 light freighter]] ''[[Ghost]]'' were named for their ability to sneak past [[Galactic Empire|Imperial]] sensors.<ref name="A New Dawn">[[A New Dawn (novel)|''A New Dawn'']]</ref>

Sensors could be divided into two categories, active or passive. Active sensors, also called search-mode sensors, detected targets by emitting controlled bursts of energy and then detecting when it reflected or "bounce" off of a target. While this allowed for detailed scanning of a target, the emitted energy would easily alert someone to its source, and their operation required relatively large amounts of power. Active sensors could be set to one of three modes:<ref name="YT1300" />
*Scan Mode: In this mode the sensor scanned the entire area around itself but could provide only basic information. Any potential hazards which were discovered triggered a warning signal to warrant a closer look.<ref name="YT1300" />
*Search Mode: When set to this mode the sensor would only look for a specific type of target as indicated by the sensor's operator. For example, ships flying in formation may set their sensors to search mode so that they only focused on specific areas. When working with a [[Navigation computer|navicomputer]], search mode could also help plot an emergency escape route.
*Focus Mode: Used to concentrate on a specific area selected by the operator, this mode could provide much more detailed information about the scanned area compared to the other modes. However it was blind to anything outside its designated scope.<ref name="YT1300" />
The second type were passive sensors, which did not emit energy and could only detect targets by the energy they emitted themselves. This did mean they required less power and were more difficult to detect when operated though.<ref name="YT1300" />

==Use==
Examples of sensors for personal use ranged from simple [[telescope]]s and [[macrobinoculars]] to more complex devices like [[electrobinoculars]] and [[radiation sensor]]s. [[Droid]]s could also possess a wide array of sensing devices. Imperial [[Probe droid]]s for example could scan for objects using visual, [[ultraviolet]] and [[magnet]]ic imaging devices.<ref name="YT1300" /><ref name="Complete Vehicle New Edition">''[[Star Wars Complete Vehicles, New Edition]]''</ref>

Many vehicles, particularly military types, were also equipped with a wide variety of sensors. [[Tank]]s such as the [[Armored Assault Tank Mk I|AAT]] might possess rangefinding devices, while many [[walker]]s like the [[All Terrain Armored Transport|AT-AT]] and [[All Terrain Scout Transport|AT-ST]] possessed terrain sensors in their feet in order help with finding sure footing. Some like the [[HAVw A6 Juggernaut]] carried special headlights that scanned for targets using both visible and invisible light.<ref name="Complete Vehicle New Edition />

In general, starships carried sensors which could scan for objects across a wide spectrum.<ref name="Complete Vehicle New Edition" /> Examples of common sensors found on starships include [[electro-photo receptor]]s, [[dedicated energy receptor]]s, [[full-spectrum transceiver]]s, and [[terrain-following sensor]]s. Most were mounted in a [[sensor array]] which combined several sensing devices with computers to analyze the collected data and present it to the operator.<ref name="YT1300" /> For example, ship sensors could detect [[cronau radiation]], which all ships emitted upon entering hyperspace,<ref name="Tarkin">[[Tarkin (novel)|''Tarkin'']]</ref> which provided a few seconds' warning of a vessel approaching from hyperspace by detecting these particle traces.<ref name="Alphabet Squadron">''[[Alphabet Squadron]]''</ref> The larger the vessel, the more powerful the sensor array, however their large size also made them easier to detect in return.<ref name="YT1300" /><ref name="Tarkin" /> Some starships like the [[BTL Y-wing starfighter]] and [[Naboo Royal Starship]] utilized the stereoscopic principal to greatly enhance the accuracy of their sensors.<ref name="Complete Vehicle New Edition" />

One type of sensor was a moisture sensor.<ref name="Path of Deceit">''[[The High Republic: Path of Deceit]]''</ref> In [[382 BBY]],<ref name="Date">''[[Star Wars: The High Republic Character Encyclopedia]]'' dates the events of ''[[The High Republic: Path of Deceit]]'' to [[382 BBY]].</ref> after a flood in the [[Path of the Open Hand]] [[Religion|cult's]] [[Path compound|compound]] on the [[Outer Rim Territories|Outer Rim]] [[planet]] [[Dalna]], the [[Evereni]] Path [[Children of the Open Hand|member]] [[Yana Ro]] installed a few moisture sensors within the compound's [[Underground caverns|underground caves]] to ensure that the next [[time]] a flood occurred, the group's members would have enough time to prepare. After Ro had also set up lights in the [[cave]]s, she [[Brain|mentally]] noted about having set up the moisture sensors, considering it a parting gift to those in the Path who had loved her as she planned to leave the group.<ref name="Path of Deceit" />

